        "pm_h": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why the clip position changes everything.",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "pm_t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Most harnesses clip on the back, which gives your dog a full-body brace to lean into. Clip the lead to the chest ring instead and their own momentum swings them sideways, back towards you.</p><ol><li><strong>Lead on the chest ring.</strong> The matching Classic Lead clips at the front.</li><li><strong>The pull becomes a turn.</strong> Forward force is redirected to the side, so pulling stops working.</li><li><strong>Nothing on the throat.</strong> The load sits on the padded chest plate.</li></ol>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
