          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I measure my dog?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Wrap a soft tape around the widest part of the ribcage, just behind the front legs. Snug, not tight. Then the neck, where a collar sits. Compare with the <a href=\"/pages/size-guide\">size guide</a>.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "fq2_2": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if my dog is between sizes?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Go up. Thick double coat? Go up. Wrong size costs you nothing: free swap within 60 days.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "fq2_3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why can a harness twist?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Twisting almost always means a size too big or the two sides tightened unevenly. Fit by chest, adjust both sides, two fingers under each strap. Steps in the <a href=\"/pages/fitting-guide\">fitting guide</a>.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "fq2_4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can the straps loosen?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Sliders can settle on the first walk. Re-check the belly strap after five minutes. If a strap keeps slipping after that, contact us; that's a fault and we replace it.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
